Read and follow the repository root `AGENTS.md` before performing any task.

## Global Workflow Commands
For workflow commands, read `.agents/WORKFLOWS.md` and then the referenced repository-local skill.

## Agent Translation (Subagent & Tier Directives)
Follow the **Multi-IDE Host Capability Matrix (Mode D — Cursor)** in `.agents/rules/multi-ide-setup.md`.

### Tool mapping
- Abstract `invoke_subagent` → Cursor native `Task` tool (never invent `invoke_subagent`).
- `TypeName: 'self'` (implementer) → `Task` with `subagent_type: "generalPurpose"`.
- `TypeName: 'research'` (Red-Team / read-only auditor) → `Task` with `subagent_type: "explore"` (or an explicit read-only prompt).
- Stream / handoff links → Cursor `[Name](agent-id)` convention (not `conversation://`).
- Living plans and cross-IDE reports → `.tmp/` (gitignored), never IDE-internal artifact storage.

### Tier behavior (no fake model slugs)
- Do **not** pass `flash_lite`, `flash`, or `pro` as Cursor `model` values. Default `model: "inherit"`. Pass a non-`inherit` slug only when the user explicitly requested a model from the session's available subagent models list.
- **Tier 1 (`FLASH_LITE`, Score 1–3) & Tier 2 (`FLASH`, Score 4–6):** Apply `.agents/skills/flash/SKILL.md` (Single-Action Protocol). Execute inline for a single matching `#exec N` step; otherwise spawn `Task` for isolation (`#exec all`, `#delegate`, `#solve`, multi-step plans).
- **Tier 3 (`PRO`, Score 7–10 or files >=500 lines):** Prefer a high-reasoning parent model; spawn `Task` with `inherit` for isolation when needed; perform an explicit self-review (or `explore` auditor when Score >= 8) before staging. Preserve the global decomposition and completeness standard.
- **Wave Execution (`#exec-wave`):** Parallel `Task` batches only when file inventories are disjoint; otherwise serial. Per-batch context isolation; consolidated validation after each wave. Enforce the 3-point completion feedback contract (`Status`, `Files Modified`, `Summary`).

### Domain rules
Before editing, Read every `.agents/rules/*.md` that matches the AGENTS.md file-to-rule table for the files you will touch.
